 "note": "Test: free Whisper word timing + word anchors (no ElevenLabs transcription) (retry)",
 "script": "Grain prices could jump as much as eighty percent. And it comes down to one strip of water. The Strait of Hormuz has been choked by the Iran war for months. About a third of the world's fertilizer trade moves through it. Now the International Chamber of Commerce warns that available fertilizer is down nearly forty percent. Two point seven million tons... gone. Less fertilizer means smaller harvests. Smaller harvests mean pricier wheat, corn and rice. Poorer countries get hit first. But grain is traded worldwide, so prices travel. Would you cut back if bread got this expensive? Tell us below."
